 ## Background
-Coarse-to-Fine Optimization was introduced in two key papers:
-1.  **Nerfies** (Park et al., 2021) [S2]: Proposed frequency annealing of positional encodings to regularize the deformation field, preventing it from overfitting to high-frequency noise early in training.
-2.  **DP-NeRF** (Zhang et al., 2022) [S1]: Proposed exponential decay of the weight between a coarse rigid background loss and a fine adaptive weighting prior loss to stabilize training for deblurred scene reconstruction.
-
-Both methods address the instability of optimizing high-capacity neural networks for complex 3D representations from scratch.
+Coarse-to-Fine Optimization was introduced in two key papers: Nerfies (Park et al., 2021) [S2] proposed frequency annealing of positional encodings to regularize the deformation field, preventing it from overfitting to high-frequency noise early in training. DP-NeRF (Zhang et al., 2022) [S1] proposed exponential decay of the weight between a coarse rigid background loss and a fine adaptive weighting prior loss to stabilize training for deblurred scene reconstruction. Both methods address the instability of optimizing high-capacity neural networks for complex 3D representations from scratch [G].
 
